<title>UKRAINE: Unpredictable effect if EMU delayed -Italy's Prodi.</title>
<headline>Unpredictable effect if EMU delayed -Italy's Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>LVOV, Ukraine 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said he saw unpredictable effects on the process of European economic and monetary union (EMU) if it were to be delayed for a long time.</p>
<p>Prodi, on a visit to Lvov in Ukraine where he met President Leonid Kuchma, said: &quot;If there was a lengthy and serious delay, then you never know what could possibly happen.&quot;  </p>
<p>Prodi was talking at a joint news conference with Kuchma.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi, speaking in Rome, said a delay to EMU could endanger monetary union, telling an upper house of parliament hearing that delay would be &quot;dangerous because it could be the start of further delays and nothing ever gets done&quot;.</p>
